{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC-2 EVIDENCE — BEDROCK live structured cache canary: RAN, PASSED.\n\nSame instrument, same byte-identical 41,360-char system prefix, same two-call write/read\nsequence, run minutes after the Anthropic arm. Authenticated from the ambient AWS chain\n(rebar manages no Bedrock key). No credential was printed, logged, or persisted.\n\nModel id (requested and ran): bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\nProvider provenance: provider=bedrock, tier=first_class, region=us-west-2\nTyped result: verdict=PASS (a valid completion_verdict)\nRunner provenance: pydantic_ai\n\nCALL 1 (write) — started 2026-08-20T00:11:13.042209+00:00, finished 2026-08-20T00:11:15.106575+00:00\n  requests            = 1\n  input_tokens        = 10747\n  output_tokens       = 34\n  cache_write_tokens  = 10685\n  cache_read_tokens   = 0\n  finish_reason       = stop\n  output_retry_allowance = 2 (none consumed)\n\nCALL 2 (read) — started 2026-08-20T00:11:15.106583+00:00, finished 2026-08-20T00:11:16.925353+00:00\n  requests            = 1\n  input_tokens        = 10747\n  output_tokens       = 34\n  cache_write_tokens  = 0\n  cache_read_tokens   = 10685\n  finish_reason       = stop\n  output_retry_allowance = 2 (none consumed)\n\nCOMPLETE-vs-OMIT BRANCH — same direct instrumentation. On each call the wire projection fired\nexactly once with messages_in = 1, messages_kept = 1, failed_output_candidates = 0,\nomitted = 0, reserve = 16000 tokens, candidate set = [\"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\"]\n=> COMPLETE branch on every request, nothing omitted; the OMIT branch was not exercised for\nthe same happy-path reason as the Anthropic arm.\n\nMEASUREMENT CAVEAT (recorded so it is not mistaken for a finding). The canary additionally\nprobed capabilities out-of-band by passing the model STRING \"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-\nsonnet-4-6\", and that probe reported prompt_cache_style=\"none\" with no cache settings. That is\nan artifact of the STRING form: bedrock deliberately has no string profile resolver (resolving\none would require boto3), so a bedrock string lands on the conservative record. The runner's\nown path passes the model OBJECT, which resolves the real Bedrock profile — and the live\ncounts prove it did: a 10,685-token cache WRITE followed by a 10,685-token cache READ cannot\noccur with caching disabled. Do not read that probe line as a Bedrock caching defect."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787184852726352001,"uuid":"40b28c11-3277-429e-82c3-a21360f894ec"}